ophy, Dennis J. Schmidt develops the question of philosophy's regard of the image in thinking by considering painting-where the image most clearly calls attention to itself as an image. Focusing on Heidegger and the work of Paul Klee, Schmidt pursues larger issues in the relationship between word, image, and truth. As he investigates alternative ways of thinking about truth through word and image, Schmidt shows how the form o"},"tableOfContents":"Introduction: the genesis of the question -- Unfolding the question: an excentric history -- Heidegger and Klee: an attempt at a new beginning -- On word, image, and gesture: another attempt at a beginning -- Afterword: the question of genesis for now.","note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Dennis J. Schmidt."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references and index."},{"@type":"language","#text":"English"}],"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Heidegger, Martin",{"@type":"date","#text":"1889-1976"}]}},{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Klee, Paul",{"@type":"date","#text":"1879-1940"}]}},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Image (Philosophy)"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Aesthetics"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Thought and thinking"}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"BH301.I52 S37 2012"},{"@edition":"23","@authority":"ddc","#text":"111/.85"}],"relatedItem":[{"titleInfo":{"title":"Studies in Continental thought"}},null,null,{"@type":"series","titleInfo":{"title":"Studies in Continental Thought"}},{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/99153596974403941/catalog"}}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9786613925947"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9781283613491"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"1283613492"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9780253006226"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"0253006228"},{"@type":"lccn","@invalid":"yes","#text":"2012022626"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"813385121"}],"locati